 ## Security & hardening roadmap
 
-Implemented: HTTPS/ACM with HTTP→HTTPS redirect, bcrypt password hashing, RDS in private subnets (not publicly accessible), secrets in Secrets Manager (not in source), least-privilege IAM for the instance role, secrets git-ignored.
+Implemented:
+
+- HTTPS/ACM with HTTP→HTTPS redirect.
+- **JWT-based authentication** (HS256): login takes a request body and returns a token; the signing key is injected from the host, not in source.
+- **Per-user authorization** on report routes — a user can only access their own reports; cross-user access returns 403 (closes an IDOR).
+- bcrypt password hashing.
+- RDS in private subnets (not publicly accessible); deletion protection enabled.
+- S3 public-access block, versioning, and default encryption.
+- Secrets in Secrets Manager (not in source); least-privilege IAM for the instance role; secrets git-ignored.
 
